WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.040
Netflix continues to be a beacon of light
for serialized genre fiction, as they are

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.799
now readying new seasons of hit series like
Stranger Things and The Umbrella Academy,

00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:12.450
and adding explosive new treats on a near
weekly basis.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:17.890
For those on the lookout for a fresh fantasy
offering, Netflix's latest is a live-action

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.950
drama based on a beloved animated series.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.720
Indeed, the Nickelodeon series which inspired
this new show is Winx Club, which follows

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.570
the adventures of five gifted teen fairies
who attend a magical boarding school and fight

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.250
evildoers in the magical realm of Otherworld.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:37.550
However, fans of Winx Club should know that
Netflix's Fate: The Winx Saga is a very different

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.120
beast than its more kid-friendly inspiration.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:45.199
Perhaps taking a cue from the recent successes
of adult-oriented teen dramas like Riverdale

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:50.100
and Chilling Adventures of Sabrina, the new
Netflix venture delivers a wild mix of bombastic

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:56.297
action, brooding teen angst, and saucy romance,
along with an inspiring journey of self-discovery.

00:00:56.297 --> 00:00:57.566
"You must be a fairy."

00:00:57.566 --> 00:00:59.566
"I am a fairy.

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:03.960
Sorry, that's just something I never thought
I would say."

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.080
The series is centered around the teen-aged
Bloom, a fairy raised by humans and sent to

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:14.240
the Alfea school so she can learn the ways
of fairies, and also to control her dangerous

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.890
magical abilities.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:20.680
And if Abigail Cowen looks familiar to you,
it's likely because you're a fan of teen dramas

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.080
with an adult bent.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.170
As it happens, another series which Cowen
appeared in also turned some heads for its

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:30.189
slightly twisted take on considerably tamer
source material.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:35.060
That series was Chilling Adventures of Sabrina,
which told the tale of a teenage girl as she

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.930
nobly, and sometimes not-so nobly, struggled
to balance her everyday life amongst humans

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:44.380
with her more exciting life as a witch, who
just so happens to worship at the altar of

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.909
a certain dark lord.

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:50.710
Essentially posited as a classic teen drama
with heaping doses of magical mirth, gory

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.979
horror movie camp, and some seriously sinister
action, Chilling Adventures of Sabrina debuted

00:01:55.979 --> 00:02:01.660
on Netflix to great reviews in 2018, and has
just wrapped an equally lauded four season

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.060
run on the platform.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:08.039
Cowen appeared in three of those seasons as
one of the Weird Sisters, a trio who frequently

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:11.220
tormented and occasionally teamed up with
Sabrina.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:15.690
If you're wondering why Cowen didn't appear
in all four seasons of the supernatural series,

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:20.470
it's because her character Dorcas tragically
didn't survive the third, having been turned

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.250
to stone, then later killed.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:26.090
Needless to say, the Weird Sisters were never
really the same after Dorcas' death.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:31.090
Likewise, Cowen's presence was sorely missed
throughout Sabrina's wonderful fourth season.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:35.640
Although, Dorcas fans were treated to a brief
resurrection during one emotional episode.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.410
"I'm back, Prudence.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:40.360
Yes, yes I see that."

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:44.050
If you haven't had a chance to watch Chilling
Adventures of Sabrina just yet, it's still

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:49.210
entirely likely you noticed Cowen's face on
Netflix before her roles as Dorcas and Bloom,

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.950
though you would have had to do so through
a waft of wavy eighties hair.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:57.500
You also would have needed to keep an exceedingly
sharp eye out for her ginger locks, as Cowen

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:01.800
made only a couple of brief appearances in
the troubled town of Hawkins, Indiana.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.970
That's right, Stranger Things fans: one of
Cowen's first appearances came in the second

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.670
season of Netflix's sci-fi sensation.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.140
Cowen actually appeared in two episodes, but
there's little question she made a far bigger

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.700
impact in the first.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:19.010
And as far as that first appearance goes,
it came in the season 2 premiere, round about

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.570
the time bad boy extraordinaire Billy Hargrove
made his infamous first trip through the parking

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.310
lot of Hawkins High School.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:29.780
As you might recall, a small group of Hawkins
girls watch the chain-smoking hard rocker

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:33.680
as he walks, commenting on his ... ahem, posterior
region.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.790
Cowen was one of those gawking girls.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:40.290
And while we don't learn much about her character,
Vicki, we do know she had at least a fleeting

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:44.850
encounter with Hawkins' baddest of bad boys,
as she's seen leaving school with him a couple

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.130
episodes later.

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:50.510
She was never again spotted in Hawkins High
though, possibly because Cowen moved on to

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.450
bigger roles, like in Sabrina.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:56.450
Whatever the case the may be, it's nice to
see Abigail Cowen is continuing her already

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:01.480
fruitful relationship with Netflix: The streamer
is reportedly eyeing a second season of Fate:

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:06.260
The Winx Saga after it debuted at #1 on their
coveted Top 10 chart.

